    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community owns two private Chesapeake Bay beaches—Driftwood Beach and Seahorse Beach—and a manmade lake called Lake Lariat.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chesapeake_Ranch_Estates%2C_Maryland"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Lake Lariat has long struggled with pollution, including runoff, algae blooms, and high mercury levels that trigger a fish‑consumption advisory.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chesapeake_Ranch_Estates%2C_Maryland"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A small airfield, a horseshoes field, a duck pond, and a campground are part of the CRE’s recreational amenities.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chesapeake_Ranch_Estates%2C_Maryland"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The cliffs near Seahorse Beach contain over 600 fossil species, but they are off‑limits because they can collapse.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chesapeake_Ranch_Estates%2C_Maryland"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Chesapeake Ranch Estates is an unincorporated community that is protected 24/7 by security guards, yet its roads remain open to all for residents and visitors.",
